+// g-lab-bit fork (filter_unchanged.patch)
+// Experimental API.
+// Function: FPDF_FilterUnchangedObjects
+//          Removes from |objnums|, in place and keeping the order, every
+//          EXISTING object (number <= the original's last object number)
+//          whose current in-memory value equals its value in the loaded
+//          file - e.g. an annotation edited and then reverted, or listed by
+//          a failed edit. Objects never loaded since the document was opened
+//          are unchanged by definition and also removed. Values are compared
+//          like FPDF_VerifyIncrementalSave() compares them (decrypted strings
+//          and streams; streams by dictionary without /Length and by data;
+//          PDFium's own post-load normalisations accepted exactly). The
+//          original value is parsed from the file without adding anything to
+//          the document's object map. New objects (created since load) are
+//          never removed; FPDF_SaveIncrementalObjects() already skips those
+//          that are not reachable. Entries that are 0 or cannot be parsed are
+//          kept (FPDF_SaveIncrementalObjects() then refuses them).
+//          If the result is 0 and nothing new is reachable, the save would be
+//          an exact copy of the original: the caller can skip writing.
+// Parameters:
+//          document - The document handle.
+//          objnums  - The list to filter; modified in place.
+//          count    - Number of entries in |objnums|.
+// Return value:
+//          The new number of entries, or -1 on error.
+FPDF_EXPORT int FPDF_CALLCONV
+FPDF_FilterUnchangedObjects(FPDF_DOCUMENT document,
+                            uint32_t* objnums,
+                            int count);
+
